Généatique, born in the 1980s and kept relevant for forty years, evolves with artificial intelligence to help genealogists process old documents. The company Mise à jour offers tools that transform the work of indexing and transcription, continuing the goal of constructing and representing genealogical trees.
The integration relies on specific data such as the SOCFACE project, which reads and indexes nominative censuses thanks to AI. This approach illustrates gains in automation while emphasizing that results remain dependent on data quality and algorithms, with limits of fidelity and context in historical records.
